Drives its own private GC state (its own `gcBindMemory`/`gcInit`-bound arena) and
every assertion is about that private heap: how many chunks two successive
same-shape bursts cost the reserve, and whether the second is bounded by the
first's -- the #3868 span free list's whole point. None of it depends on
whether the ambient (libbitrt) collector ever runs; the objects it allocates
are the private collector's and invisible to the ambient one.
